=== pretty-printed JSON, as GCS answers a 429
{ "error": { "code": 429, "message": "The rate of change requests to the object exceeds the limit.", "status": "RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED" } }

=== an nginx error page
<html> <head><title>502 Bad Gateway</title></head> <body> <center><h1>502 Bad Gateway</h1></center> <hr><center>nginx/1.24.0</center> </body> </html>

=== one line, short enough to stand on its own
InvalidAccessKeyId: the key is not on file

=== a body longer than the limit, on one line
xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx ...

=== an XML error, as S3 answers
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?> <Error><Code>SlowDown</Code><Message>Please reduce your request rate.</Message></Error>

=== empty
(empty)

=== whitespace only
(empty)

